From ed6f51019d9a4d486e1d5edd18aa6779c5a83894 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:35:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Upkeep U2: e1000 EEPROM (EERD) + PHY register file (MDIC)

Upkeep U0 measured that EERD (0x14) and MDIC were generic
storage cells: the frozen guest's EEPROM probe for words 0-2
polled a DONE bit that could never set -- three 100,000-poll
timeouts on every probe, with the MAC then arriving from
RAL/RAH -- and MDIC only echoed the fictional command dword
to any driver that probed the PHY.

The device now has the hardware behind both registers,
measured from QEMU hw/net/e1000.c, e1000x_common.c and
Intel's e1000x_regs.h, per this model's QEMU-parity ground
rule:

- EEPROM: the 64-word e1000_eeprom_template prepared
  e1000x_core_prepare_eeprom-style (MAC 52:54:00:12:34:56 in
  words 0-2, 0x100E in words 11/13, word 0x3F closing the sum
  to 0xBABA), once at device add.  EERD stores are plain;
  the read mirrors flash_eerd_read (synchronous DONE on the
  first poll, unmasked address shift, addresses past 0x3F
  complete with the stored data field).  The expected guest
  receipt change is that its probe now names the EEPROM as
  the MAC source; the address is the same.
- PHY: a 32-register M88E1000 file at MDIC PHY address 1
  under QEMU's phy_regcap table, seeded with phy_reg_init
  (PHYID2 0x0C20 for the 82540EM) at the autonegotiation-
  done steady state QEMU reaches through its 500ms timer.
  Our link is permanently up (STATUS.LU from reset), so
  ANRESTART completes synchronously; no link flap is
  fabricated.  MDIC mirrors set_mdic branch for branch:
  READY on every store; ERROR for read-only/unimplemented
  registers and for a wrong PHY address (echoing the
  previous MDIC value); BMCR through set_phy_ctrl's mask
  (RESET/ANRESTART self-clear, the file not reset);
  INT_EN raises the MDAC cause onto the N4 INTx wire.
- The MDIC register moved to Intel's offset 0x20; N0's
  0x200 was a typo no consumer could observe.

The EECD Microwire bit-bang stays a plain register (no
measured consumer touches it), and machine_t does not move:
the new state lives in e1000_t and --tap runs already refuse
snapshots.

Vectors (tests/test_net.c, 2 new groups): the guest's exact
EERD probe returns the MAC with first-poll DONE; identity
words; the 64-word 0xBABA sum read back through EERD;
out-of-range and START-clear behaviour; EEPROM surviving
CTRL.RST.  MDIC ID/status/template values, RW round-trips,
OP=0/OP=3 branch order, ERROR paths (read-only,
unimplemented, wrong PHY with previous-value echo), the
BMCR mask with the file intact, MDAC onto the INTx pin,
and reset restoring the PHY template.  All pre-U2 groups
and the N1/N2/N3 lanes pass unchanged.  NC: e1000.c at U1
-- behavioural abort at the EERD DONE assert after the full
100,000-poll timeout.  Gates: make test (incl. network e2e)
and make test-sanitize green; both SeaBIOS ISO lanes green
for real.
